/Alt (Bicyclist Design User Profiles measures a scale of Low Stress Tolerance on the left and High Stress Tolerance on the right. User Profiles are divided into three sections. The first and leftmost section represents Interested but Concerned being 51 to 56 percent of the total population with accompanying text, Often not comfortable with bike lanes, may bike on sidewalks even if bike lanes are provided; prefer off-street or separated bicycle fatalities or quiet or traffic-calmed residential roads. May not bike at all if bicycle facilities do not meet needs for perceived comfort. The second and middle section represents Somewhat Confident being 5 to 9 percent of the total population with accompanying text, Generally prefer more separated facilities, but are comfortable riding in bicycle lanes or on paved shoulders if need be. The third and rightmost section represents Highly Confident being 4 to 7 percent of the total population with accompanying text Comfortable riding with traffic; will use roads without bike lanes. Additionally, profile shows six bicyclists ranging from a child to an experienced bicyclist.)
/K 3
/P 18 0 R
